    k: 'Hikoya', t: 'The Email That Went to Everyone', s: 'Bir bosishdagi xato va undan olingan saboq',
    p: [
      ['Kamola worked in a big company, and she faced a [dilemma] every morning: a stressful job or a safe one. She was good at her work, but she could be [hasty] and sometimes [reckless] with emails. Her top [priority] was to finish things fast. Once she wrote to her manager: “I will tell the truth about the project.” She clicked send without a thought. It was an [impulse], and it became a huge [blunder]. She had [overlooked|overlook] one detail: the address.',
       'Kamola katta kompaniyada ishlardi va har tong qiyin tanlov oldida turardi: stressli ish yoki xavfsiz ish. U o‘z ishida yaxshi edi, lekin shoshqaloq va ba’zan xatlarda beparvo bo‘lardi. Eng muhim ustuvorligi ishni tez tugatish edi. Bir marta u menejeriga yozdi: «Men loyiha haqida haqiqatni aytaman.» U o‘ylamasdan yuborish tugmasini bosdi. Bu ichki turtki edi va katta xatoga aylandi. U bitta tafsilotni — manzilni e’tibordan chetda qoldirgan edi.'],
      ['The email went to the whole company. It was a terrible [oversight], not a [deliberately] planned action, but the [consequence] was [disastrous]. A [misunderstanding] began: people thought she was criticising the director. Kamola felt [mortified] and [regretful]. Her [judgement] had failed, and she felt deep [regret]. “If I had checked the address, this would never have happened,” she cried. Her friend said, “Don’t [blame] yourself, and don’t [cry over spilt milk|cry over spilt milk]. It’s [not the end of the world|it’s not the end of the world].”',
       'Xat butun kompaniyaga ketdi. Bu ataylab qilingan harakat emas, dahshatli e’tiborsizlik edi, lekin oqibat halokatli bo‘ldi. Tushunmovchilik boshlandi: odamlar u direktorni tanqid qilyapti deb o‘ylashdi. Kamola xijolat bo‘ldi va afsuslandi. Uning bahosi xato chiqdi va u chuqur pushaymon bo‘ldi. «Manzilni tekshirganimda, bu hech qachon bo‘lmasdi», deb yig‘ladi u. Do‘sti dedi: «O‘zingni ayblama va o‘tgan ishga achinma. Dunyoning oxiri emas.»'],
      ['She decided to [make amends|make amends] publicly. First she wanted to find an [excuse], but she realised that was wrong. She chose to [admit] her mistake and wrote a sincere [apology]. She did not [hesitate]. Instead of looking for [alternatives|alternative], she [weighed up|weigh up] the pros and cons: to hide or to be honest? She had [second thoughts|second thoughts], but it was a [wise] decision. She had [misjudged|misjudge] people’s reaction.',
       'U hammaning oldida uzr so‘rashga qaror qildi. Avval u bahona topmoqchi bo‘ldi, lekin bu noto‘g‘ri ekanini tushundi. U xatosini tan olishni tanladi va samimiy uzr yozdi. U ikkilanmadi. Muqobil izlash o‘rniga, foyda va zararni taqqosladi: yashirish yoki halol bo‘lish? U ikkilanib qoldi, lekin bu dono qaror edi. U odamlarning munosabatini noto‘g‘ri baholagan edi.'],
      ['To her surprise, colleagues respected her honesty. The director laughed: “I made a bigger [blunder] last year.” It was a hard lesson with a clear [moral], but also a good [opportunity] to learn. “I [learned the hard way|learn the hard way],” Kamola said later. [Regrettably], she could not change the past. But in [hindsight], the [failure] and the [setback] made her wiser. Now she [thinks twice|think twice], and before she acts, she doesn’t [jump the gun|jump the gun].',
       'Hayratlanarlisi, hamkasblar uning halolligini hurmat qilishdi. Direktor kuldi: «Men o‘tgan yili bundan kattaroq xato qilgandim.» Bu og‘ir saboq edi, lekin o‘rganish uchun yaxshi imkoniyat ham edi. «Men buni og‘ir yo‘l bilan o‘rgandim», dedi Kamola keyinroq. Afsuski, o‘tmishni o‘zgartirib bo‘lmasdi. Lekin orqaga qarab, muvaffaqiyatsizlik va to‘siq uni dono qildi. Endi u ikki bor o‘ylaydi va harakat qilishdan oldin shoshilmaydi.']
    ],
